Subject: [PATCH] btu_hcif: do not mark the link encrypted before its key size is read

"Enforce incoming CTKD security requirements" (LineageOS lineage-20.0, September 2026,
a combined backport from Main) marks a BR/EDR link encrypted as soon as the controller
reports encryption on, before the stack has read the key size. When the key size
comes back, btm_sec_encrypt_change() finds the link authenticated and encrypted and,
in Android 13's version of it, returns early: "Link is authenticated & encrypted,
ignoring this enc change event". That early return also skips what wakes the
channels waiting for encryption. After a pairing, SDP still works, because it needs no
security, but the A2DP and HFP channels are never opened: the L2CAP connection
request does not reach the air, and Android gives up after 30 seconds. Seen with
Galaxy Buds3 FE, which had worked before the merge.

This takes out the early marking and keeps the rest of the change. An incoming CTKD
request that arrives before the key size is read is then refused; this controller
(Bluetooth 4.1, no Secure Connections) has its CTKD refused by the same change anyway.
---
diff --git a/system/stack/btu/btu_hcif.cc b/system/stack/btu/btu_hcif.cc
index d522662..31bc9b4 100644
--- a/system/stack/btu/btu_hcif.cc
+++ b/system/stack/btu/btu_hcif.cc
@@ -1085,12 +1085,6 @@ static void btu_hcif_encryption_change_evt(uint8_t* p) {
     btm_sec_encrypt_change(handle, static_cast<tHCI_STATUS>(status),
                            encr_enable);
   } else {
-    // CTKD request from the remote central device will get rejected if the link is "not"
-    // encrypted. So we should mark the link as encrypted immediately.
-    tBTM_SEC_DEV_REC* p_dev_rec = btm_find_dev_by_handle(handle);
-    if (p_dev_rec != nullptr) {
-      p_dev_rec->set_device_encrypted();
-    }
     btsnd_hcic_read_encryption_key_size(
         handle,
         base::Bind(&read_encryption_key_size_complete_after_encryption_change));
